      "a": "<p>P(W) = 0.6(0.3) + 0.05(0.7) = 0.215, so P(S | W) = 0.18/0.215 ≈ 0.837.</p>\n<p>With a 1% spam rate: P(W) = 0.006 + 0.0495 = 0.0555, so P(S | W) ≈ 0.108.</p>\n<p>Same word, 0.84 versus 0.11 — the evidence did not change, the prior did.</p>",
