     {
      "q": "Your self-rating is Fluency 4, Accuracy 3, Range 2, Pronunciation 3, Coherence 4, Interaction 2. Choose one target for the next fortnight, justify it with evidence, and write a five-line practice plan plus the AI prompt you would use.",
      "a": "<p>Model answer:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Target: Interaction (2).</strong> Evidence: in the rubric, interaction 2 means \"monologue or silence\" — and this is the lowest score with the highest interview cost, because a candidate who does not build on others or check understanding reads as a poor collaborator regardless of fluency. Range (2) is the second priority and can be folded into the same drill by forcing one precise word per turn.</li><li>Justification against the alternative: Pronunciation (3) is not blocking communication; fluency (4) and coherence (4) are already adequate, so drilling them yields little.</li><li><strong>Practice plan:</strong></li><li>Daily 10 min: answer one question, then add one <em>building</em> sentence (\"that connects to…\") and one <em>checking</em> question (\"does that answer it?\").</li><li>Twice weekly: 4/3/2 on the same topic, with a rule of ending each turn by handing over.</li><li>Weekly: one 15-minute conversation with a senior; ask them to note every time you interrupted or went silent.</li><li>Record and count: turns per conversation, and questions asked per conversation.</li><li>Re-rate in 14 days with written evidence per row.</li><li><strong>AI prompt:</strong> <em>\"Act as a conversation partner on 'my final-year project'. Ask me one question at a time and wait. After each of my answers, do not praise me — instead note whether I (a) built on my previous point, (b) asked you anything. At the end, give me the count of my turns and questions, and three phrases I could have used to hand the turn back.\"</em></li></ul>",
      "tag": "exam",
      "qHtml": "Your self-rating is Fluency 4, Accuracy 3, Range 2, Pronunciation 3, Coherence 4, Interaction 2. Choose one target for the next fortnight, justify it with evidence, and write a five-line practice plan plus the AI prompt you would use."
     }
